{
  "schema": "walk_tuning@v1",
  "notes": "walk_tuning.json with imp = 3 (round 4 step 9.4b): the sagittal whole-body QP (Tools/GaitOpt/qp_proto/controller_fid.py, b5 preset) writes the feed-forward of the six sagittal leg DOFs on top of the imp 2 pipeline; scenarios load this file explicitly. walk_tuning.json stays imp 0. Lengths as fractions of leg length l (hip height, 42 m at reference), speeds via Froude number or l/t*, times in t* = sqrt(l/g) (2.07 s), accelerations in g, forces in body weights. R-001: fr band 0.10-0.30, cruise 0.20, stride = 2.3 Fr^0.3 l (Alexander), duty 0.60-0.72, start <= 0.14 g, normal stop 1.5-3 steps, emergency stop <= 0.30 g, lateral <= 0.085 g, yaw rate <= 26.7 deg/s and yaw accel <= 4 deg/s^2 at l = 42.4 m (stored here in t* units: 55.5 deg/t*, 17.3 deg/t*^2, used at 80 %). R-005 section 5.2: height loop 0.3 Hz, CoP 10 % inside the sole, swing clearance 3-5 m, touchdown <= 1 m/s, attitude loop 0.5 Hz. Everything else is controller tuning found on the reference mech (Assumed). Round 2 (research/R-008): imp = 1 switches the walking stance to joint impedance around the state-indexed stance posture (StancePosture): hip height imp_hip_height_frac of the leg length, smallest stance knee flexion, ankle margin inside its range, largest heel-strike and toe-off pitches (R-008 section 1: 25 and 20-40 degrees), leg-length stiffness as a vertical natural frequency (imp_leg_hz, imp_leg_zeta) mapped to the knee and, on a rocker, to the ankle (imp_ankle_hz), pelvic tilt about 10 degrees at full rollover. yaw_budget_*: R-008 friction budget for the stance foot's free moment, 1.65e8 N m flat and 0.85e8 on a heel or toe line at one body weight, as fractions of weight x leg length. id_*: feed-forward from the engine's inverse dynamics (gravity, Coriolis and centrifugal, inertia x reference acceleration).",
